body:
I have found a workaround for this using animation params. I don't know if this would be useful for you @konstantintieber. I hope yes:

```
const fadeIn = this._animationBuilder.build([
  style({ opacity: 0 }),
  animate('300ms {{delay}} ease-in-out', style({ opacity: 1 }))
]);
```

and then:

`
this._tooltipFadeInPlayer = fadeIn.create(this._tooltipElement, { params: { delay: '300ms' }});
`

Can also be used in this way: 

```
export const myAnimation = animation([
  animate('250ms {{delay}} cubic-bezier(0.25, 0.46, 0.45, 0.94)', style({ opacity: 1 }))
]);
```

and then: 

```
@Component({
  trigger('openClose', [
    transition('open => closed', [
      useAnimation(myAnimation, {
        params: { delay: '300ms' }
      })
    ])
  ])
})
```
